T*
(5.3 Versioning) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Event names are stable business facts, not implementation names.) Tj
T*
(- Schema versions use semantic versioning.) Tj
T*
(- Consumers must tolerate additive fields.) Tj
T*
(- Breaking changes create a new major version and dual-publish during migration.) Tj
T*
(- A schema registry stores JSON Schema/OpenAPI/AsyncAPI definitions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5.4 Retry and idempotency) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Producers attach deterministic idempotency_key values.) Tj
T*
(- Event ingestion is at-least-once; consumers must be idempotent.) Tj
T*
(- Failed deliveries go to dead-letter queues with replay tooling.) Tj
T*
(- Consumer checkpoints are stored per consumer group.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5.5 Security) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Events are signed by producers or delivered through authenticated infrastructure.) Tj
T*
(- Event payloads are classified: public, internal, restricted, highly restricted.) Tj
T*
(- PII is minimized; sensitive artifacts are referenced by secure object IDs rather than ) Tj
T*
(embedded.) Tj
T*
(- Domain authorization applies to event subscriptions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5.6 Retention and replay) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Canonical events are immutable.) Tj
T*
(- Long-term evidence events are retained for the lifetime required by product, legal, and ) Tj
T*
(institutional policy.) Tj
T*
(- Retention is domain-specific and country-aware.) Tj
T*
(- Replay can rebuild graph projections, dashboards, analytics aggregates, and passports.) Tj
ET
endstream
