stream
BT
/F1 9 Tf
13 TL
45 748 Td
() Tj
T*
(6. Anti-Corruption Layer) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The Learning Anti-Corruption Layer is the permanent translation boundary between Open edX and ) Tj
T*
(Syrka.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(flowchart LR) Tj
T*
(    OEX[Open edX native DB/APIs/events] --> EXTRACT[Extractors]) Tj
T*
(    EXTRACT --> MAP[Mapping Registry]) Tj
T*
(    MAP --> VALIDATE[Validation]) Tj
T*
(    VALIDATE --> TRANSFORM[Transformation]) Tj
T*
(    TRANSFORM --> CANON[Canonical Event Builder]) Tj
T*
(    CANON --> BUS[Syrka Event Bus]) Tj
T*
(    VALIDATE --> DLQ[Dead Letter Queue]) Tj
T*
(    DLQ --> OPS[Ops Review & Replay]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Mapping. Open edX courses, blocks, submissions, grades, discussions, and enrollment records ) Tj
T*
(are mapped to Syrka canonical identifiers using a mapping registry. The registry stores ) Tj
T*
(source_system, source_id, canonical_id, entity_type, valid_from, and valid_to.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Validation. The ACL validates source completeness, tenant ownership, consent/policy basis, ) Tj
T*
(schema compatibility, timestamp sanity, duplicate status, and required evidence references.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Transformation. The ACL converts Open edX concepts into canonical Syrka facts. Example: an ) Tj
T*
(Open edX problem attempt becomes QuizCompleted or AssessmentAttempted, not an Open edX-) Tj
T*
(specific event.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Error handling. Invalid records are rejected into a dead-letter queue with source pointer, ) Tj
T*
(validation errors, adapter version, and replay eligibility. Poison messages are quarantined.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Monitoring. Metrics include extraction lag, transform error rate, event publish success, ) Tj
T*
