(14. Architecture Principles) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. LMSs are replaceable. No strategic Syrka domain may depend on LMS-specific schemas or APIs.) Tj
T*
(2. Syrka owns all intelligence. Capabilities, inference, graphs, recommendations, passports, ) Tj
T*
(and mobility decisions are Syrka-owned.) Tj
T*
(3. Events are immutable. Corrections are new events, not mutations of history.) Tj
T*
(4. Every capability must have evidence. Capability claims without evidence are drafts or ) Tj
T*
(hypotheses, never verified facts.) Tj
T*
(5. No AI decision without provenance. Model outputs require evidence references, model ) Tj
T*
(version, confidence, explanation, and audit record.) Tj
T*
(6. Every domain has one owner. Shared ownership is forbidden. Read models and references are ) Tj
T*
(allowed.) Tj
T*
(7. APIs are contracts. Domains integrate through versioned APIs/events, not database access.) Tj
T*
(8. Domain models are independent of implementation. Supabase, Open edX, graph DBs, and LLM ) Tj
T*
(providers are implementation choices.) Tj
T*
(9. Consent is a product primitive. User-controlled data sharing must be explicit, revocable, ) Tj
T*
(and auditable.) Tj
T*
(10. Privacy is designed in. Minimize data, classify payloads, and separate artifacts from ) Tj
T*
(event metadata.) Tj
T*
(11. Security follows the data. Authorization is based on user, tenant, role, purpose, consent,) Tj
T*
( and jurisdiction.) Tj
T*
(12. Country independence is mandatory. Country overlays may specialize policy, but global ) Tj
T*
(architecture remains stable.) Tj
T*
(13. Institution independence is mandatory. Institutions configure mappings and policies; they ) Tj
T*
(do not fork Syrka semantics.) Tj
T*
(14. AI vendors are replaceable. Prompt templates, evaluations, schemas, and provenance are ) Tj
T*
(Syrka IP; providers are adapters.) Tj
T*
(15. Reproducibility matters. Inference runs must be replayable or explainably non-replayable ) Tj
T*
(when models are deprecated.) Tj
T*
(16. Observability is required. Every event, API, worker, model run, and adapter must emit ) Tj
T*
(logs, metrics, and traces.) Tj
T*
(17. Human review exists for high-impact decisions. Mobility, credential disputes, and adverse ) Tj
T*
(opportunity decisions require appeal paths.) Tj
T*
(18. Data lineage is non-negotiable. Every derived object must point to source events and ) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
